      "status": "fixed",
      "status_notes": "CVE-2026-32285 (GHSA-6g7g-w4f8-9c9x, GO-2026-4514): the Delete function of github.com/buger/jsonparser does not validate offsets on malformed JSON, so a negative slice index panics and crashes the program. It is fixed in 1.1.2: https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-6g7g-w4f8-9c9x, https://pkg.go.dev/vuln/GO-2026-4514. Read the Go build information of every Go program in every published build-fips package for Alpine 3.23 (2.6.4-r0 to 2.28.0-r5, 86 versions, x86_64 and aarch64, from the DHI FIPS package repository); its Go programs are /usr/bin/build in every build, /opt/docker/dhi/yq from 2.26.2-r1 and /usr/bin/dhi-source from 2.28.0-r1. Every build before 2.9.0-r0 contains github.com/buger/jsonparser 1.1.1, inside the affected range; 2.9.0-r0 and every later build contain 1.1.2, which carries the fix. /opt/docker/dhi/yq does not contain the module."
